DevOps role interviews and came across these interesting questions at 'Netflix':

🔍 Round 1 – Technical Deep Dive
  ✅ How would you design CI/CD for 1000+ parallel deployments safely?
  ✅ A pod is running but refuses TCP connections – how do you debug?
  ✅ How do you handle GPU scheduling in EKS (or GKE)?
  ✅ How do you implement secure multi-tenant namespaces in Kubernetes?
  ✅ What are the scale limits of kube-proxy iptables, and how do you fix them?

🛠️ Round 2 – RCA, Outage Drills & Streaming Chaos
  🌍 How do you troubleshoot latency spikes in South America?
  🔗 How do you detect and resolve half-open TCP connections from a service mesh?
  💰 How do you investigate a NAT Gateway cost spike?

🎯 Round 3 – Leadership, Culture & Chaos Influence
  🔥 How would you run a chaos drill during a launch rehearsal?
  ⚖️ How do you balance cost efficiency vs. high availability pre-warming?
  📋 What’s your pre-flight checklist for Netflix-scale infrastructure?
  👀 Why is observability debt equal to tech debt, and how do you address it?
